Vendored commit: e9488296a44211c42701ff71705b7901470ec78f
License: MIT (see LICENSE)
Copyright (c) 2026 Ryan

Vendored files (ANATUP, unmodified except for the import paths noted below):

kit/
- iso-kit.mjs         isometric SVG geometry + shading
- iso.css             the kit's own CSS (--anatomy-* tokens)
- lathe.mjs           profile / curve math used by audit.mjs and turn-build.mjs
- tube.mjs            tube path math used by audit.mjs and turn-build.mjs
- audit.mjs           geometry audit: no clipping, every endpoint supported, draw order
- gl.mjs              optional WebGL shader camera
- gl-shared.mjs       WebGL shader helpers shared by gl.mjs and the examples
- canvas-painter.mjs  turning 3D painter used by turn-fixed.mjs
- turn.mjs            3D mode runtime (turning groups, TURN.mount, TURN_CSS)
- turn-build.mjs      3D mode builder (T.prism/round/lathe/ball/tube, painter's order)
- turn-audit.mjs      3D orbit audit (separation, cycles, layers, rigid, folds, …)
- turn-fixed.mjs      3D "fixed picture" recorder used by turn-build.mjs

scripts/
- capture.mjs         headless Chrome screenshot (clip to .iso-plate)
- drive.mjs           headless Chrome driver: wait, move, click, key, shot, lines, sheet, orbit, turn
- lines.mjs           floating-line check, wraps drive.mjs
- line-ends.mjs       LINE_ENDS: floating-line detection used by drive.mjs and turn-check.mjs
- chrome-port.mjs     reads the DevTools port from a freshly started Chrome
- inline-kit.mjs      embeds kit source into a standalone page
- turn-check.mjs      3D browser checks (--order, --pops, --lines, --perf, --fidelity)
- turn-fidelity.mjs   kit-fidelity reference used by turn-check.mjs --fidelity

references/            craft.md, kit.md, motion.md, verify.md, webgl.md, 3d.md
examples/              dial-indicator/, ripple-tank/, turning-dial/ (sources + light build)

Not vendored on purpose: kit/react/ and references/react.md (Hevi does not use
React for figures), kit/iso-kit.ts (the .mjs is the runtime), examples that are
not used as regression baselines, evals/, agents/, tests/ and SKILL.md.

Changes to vendored code: none. The only edits are the import paths the
examples and scripts need to run from this layout (they already use relative
`../../kit/...` paths upstream, so no rewrite was required), plus the light
build outputs under examples/ which are generated, not hand-edited.

Hevi uses these to build static isometric SVG figures, to run the upstream
geometry audit (audit.mjs), the floating-line check (lines.mjs), the 3D orbit
audit (turn-audit.mjs) and the 3D browser checks (turn-check.mjs), and to drive
headless Chrome (CPU / SwiftShader) for frame-by-frame video rendering.

This product bundles the Anatomy kit (MIT). The rest of the Hevi worktree is
governed by its own license.
